<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) CUTS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) CUTS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) will decrease gasoline and diesel prices by 0.60 and 4.30 drachmas per litre resprectively, effective on Thursday. Heating fuel prices will be slashed 4.50 drachmas, it said.</p>
<p>The price adjustments come after lower world gasoline and diesel prices, down by $4.0 and $17.7 per metric tonne despite a firmer dollar/drachma exchange rate, DEP said. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
